# --- KNOWN HAZARD in an imported file -------------------------------------
# qatouch-client.sh line 49:
#
#     qt_project() { printf '%s' "${QATOUCH_PROJECT:-MeLq}"; }
#
# The default is the ADVANCE project. If QATOUCH_PROJECT is ever unset — a build
# step that forgets to source env.community.sh, a local shell, a cron — every
# QA Touch call silently targets MeLq instead of NEXQ, and QA Touch has no
# delete-case endpoint to undo cases written into the wrong project.
#
# DO NOT fix this by editing qatouch-client.sh; that forks the file. Fix it at
# the two places that are ours:
#   1. ci/qa/env.community.sh sets QATOUCH_PROJECT=NEXQ  (commit 2)
#   2. build step 00 asserts it is set AND equals NEXQ before anything runs:
#        [ "${QATOUCH_PROJECT:-}" = NEXQ ] || { echo "wrong QA Touch project" >&2; exit 1; }
#
# Every other MeLq mention in that file is prose in a comment and is harmless.

